E6.4 - Evidence Cross-Check for Implementation Status
Tool Specs
Scope and Audience
This document explains the current Step 6 evidence cross-check flow used to assess prior implementation status.
Audience:
•	DS leads and SMEs reviewing evidence quality
•	step owners and teammates maintaining experiment logic
•	architecture and dev teams planning runtime hardening
Primary goals:
•	show the active retrieval and completion-review workflow
•	clarify where FSR and ER evidence are used
•	describe entry points, helper modules, and output contracts
•	capture current findings and open uncertainties
Active Anchors
Primary service-history orchestrator:
•	code_assets/runtime/service_history_completion.py
Shared retrieval and completion helpers:
•	code_assets/runtime/fsr_completion.py
Step 6 caller:
•	code_assets/experiments/step6/run_gt_til_applicability_eval.py
Reference probe module (diagnostic, not current mainline):
•	code_assets/experiments/step6/fsr_cross_reference/step6_til_fsr.py
Pipeline Map (Current)
 
Data Workflow and Process
1.	Step 6 builds a service-history request from case row, profile context, and template coverage context.
2.	Service-history module derives retrieval policy from disposition and recurring indicators.
3.	Module runs multi-branch retrieval query construction (identifier, line items, completion criteria cues).
4.	Vector retrieval attempts FSR and ER branches.
5.	If FSR is missing in vector results, SQL fallback fetches FSR rows from chunk table.
6.	Evidence rows are merged, reranked, grouped to report-level, and summarized.
7.	Completion-review LLM evaluates prior completion/open/deferred signals from summarized evidence.
8.	Final payload contains prior_service_evidence and completion_review as separate but related tracks.
